WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
- Congratulations, this is really awesome.

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:03.480
You're officially a college graduate.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.250
That's amazing that you went back,

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.313
nobody does that.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.130
- You know what I did?

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.870
I kind of never really left school.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:15.640
And my teachers, like when I was taking

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.280
a leave of absence to start working

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.510
and to do "The Village"
and stuff like that.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:20.637
I kept saying to my teachers, I'm like,

00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:21.747
"I'm gonna come back, I'm gonna come back,

00:00:21.747 --> 00:00:23.090
"I'm gonna come back."

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.960
And right away, I started taking classes

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.720
at an accredited university
in order to transfer

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.250
to eventually graduate.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.530
I didn't think it was
gonna take me 21 years.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.800
(laughing)

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.010
- Yeah well, you've been a little busy

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.030
making huge, successful movies.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.100
So yeah, not that they need to be huge

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.840
and successful, but they are.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.870
So I just think it's awesome.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.120
My mom's a teacher so when I told her

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.300
I wasn't going to college
and I was gonna be

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.930
a waitress living on a
mattress to be a singer,

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.128
it wasn't the best thing she'd ever heard.

00:00:52.128 --> 00:00:53.190
(laughing)

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.910
She wasn't very excited about the notion.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.987
So it worked out luckily.
- Yeah, yeah it did.

00:00:57.987 --> 00:00:59.430
- So how did you celebrate?

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:00.980
'Cause so many things,
like I had my birthday

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:02.870
in quarantine, everybody's
had like moments.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.330
Anniversaries, stuff like that happening

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.060
in quarantine, how'd you
celebrate graduating?

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.590
- Do you know what, it was
really kind of amazing.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.560
Like my parents got one of those things,

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.050
one of those signs that you can like

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.810
put in the grass in front of your house

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:19.290
that's like "Congratulations
Graduate Bryce"

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.264
or whatever, (laughing)

00:01:20.264 --> 00:01:21.097
- Oh my gosh,

00:01:21.097 --> 00:01:21.930
that's so southern.
- They're like parents

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:26.270
that have a graduate and I had,

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.040
my husband sent off this
thing called Tribute

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.850
where you can just like record tributes

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.960
for people and so he's sent it

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.760
to all of my friends and family

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.340
and folks that I've known
forever and ever and ever

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.420
and they all recorded
videos just, you know,

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.600
being lovely and
congratulating me and all that.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:45.700
- That's really sweet.

